nt; he also stated he feels good using his skills to make a difference.\n  - video games: Nate won a Valorant tournament championship last Saturday, is preparing for others, enjoys 'Xeonoblade Chronicles', and is creating YouTube content for video games.\n  - gaming tournaments: Nate's game tournament was pushed back. He did not make it to the finals but plans to join a new gaming team after his next tournament.\n  - Valorant: Nate won the final of a big Valorant tournament last Saturday. He continues to prepare for other tournaments, though Joanna incorrectly assumed it was a Japanese game series.\n  - Nate: Nate won a major Valorant tournament last Saturday, felt strong emotions, and is currently busy preparing for other tournaments.\n  - games: Nate won a big Valorant tournament last Saturday, enjoys gaming as an escape, finds it rewarding, and is a big fan of Nintendo games recommended by friends.\n  - high scores: Nate is helping friends reset their high scores at the international video game tournament, an activity Joanna encouraged him to continue.\n  - Nate: Nate made homemade coconut ice cream with sprinkles. His game tournament was postponed, and he didn't make the finals. He creates YouTube gaming content. He expressed support for Joanna filming her movie.\n  - tournament: Nate's game tournament was pushed back, and he did not make it to the finals. He plans to win the next time.\n  - setback: Nate experienced a setback in a video game tournament after previously winning an international tournament. Joanna expressed sympathy for the setback.\n  - Nate: Nate praised Joanna for setting up meetings with movie producers, comparing her success to winning a video game tournament, and expressed pride in her feeling hopeful and inspired.\n  - gaming: Nate's game tournament was postponed, and he did not make it to the finals, but he intends to compete again.\n  - Nate: Nate congratulated Joanna on filming her movie from the road-trip script and asked about the coo