congratulated her.\n  - store: Gina's store faced hurdles sourcing trendy pieces; she overcame this by networking and reaching out to others for contacts and products. The store plans to work with fashion bloggers/influencers.\n  - amazing products: Gina found amazing products for her store through networking and reaching out to people in her field after sourcing trendy pieces became a hurdle.\n  - Gina: Gina owns a clothing store, built a new website, encouraged Jon about his dance studio, and told Jon to \"Just do it!\" after joking about Shia LaBeouf.\n  - wholesalers: Gina emailed wholesalers for her clothing store, and one replied affirmatively, allowing her to expand and get closer to customers.\n  - biz: Jon is promoting his business and asked Gina for marketing tips. Gina suggested using social media and working with influencers for better reach.\n  - ads: Gina plans to do more ads to reach more people and build her online store's customer base.\n  - new offers and promotions: Gina is using new offers and promotions in her online store, which customers love, to drive sales and grow her customer base while starting her business.\n  - online store: Gina is growing the customer base for her online store, finding the work tough but remaining determined. She plans to work with fashion bloggers/influencers and run more ads.\n  - stuff: Gina's clothing store has its 'stuff' on display, and Jon congratulated her on how great it looks and the payoff of her hard work.\n  - my own biz: Gina was noticed by fashion editors. Jon is going full-time with his biz idea after losing his job and is learning marketing/analytics tools to advance it.\n  - Gina: Gina is keeping up with fashion trends to offer the best pieces to customers and is enjoying running her business.\n  - Gina: Gina designed a cozy and inviting space for her store. Jon congratulated her on finding the perfect spot for her store.\n  - Gina: Gina started an online clothing store after losing her job to take control of her destiny. The journey has been tough but rewarding. She encouraged Jon to believe in himself.\n  - sales: Gina is focused on growing her customer base, seeing more sales due to new offers and promotions on her online store, and looking for unique, trendy pieces.\n  - fashion mag: Gina got the idea for a new fashion piece for her store from a fashion magazine.\n  - trendy pieces: Gina sourced trendy pieces for her store after facing hurdles with sourcing, advising Jon to network for help and contacts.\n  - own business: Gina runs an online clothing store and plans influencer collaborations and ads. Jon runs a dance studio, invests much time, and learns with his successful students.\n  - fashion fans: Gina is focused on making her online store a top destination for fashion fans.\n  - fashion bloggers: Gina plans to work with fashion bloggers and influencers in the next few months to get more attention for her online store.\n  - dance-inspired items: Gina is adding dance-inspired items to her online store to show creativity and share her passion for dance and fashion.\n  - Gina: Gina built a new customer ordering website, offered support to Jon about his dance studio struggles, and plans to manage his social media and create content.\n  - Gina: Gina designed her cozy, inviting store herself, featuring trendy pieces and comfy furniture. A chandelier adds a glam feel to the space designed for customers.\n  - Gina: Gina advises Jon on marketing, is growing her online store, and asked Jon when he is opening his dance studio. She expressed excitement for his studio opening.\n  - Gina: Gina built a new website for customer orders and encouraged Jon about his dance studio challenges. She was referenced by Jon and identified as Shia Labeouf.\n  - fashion piece: Gina developed a video presentation to teach how to style her fashion pieces and mentioned it to Jon, who is starting a dance studio.\n  - marketing: Gina advised Jon to use Instagram and TikTok for marketi