stribution, and Nate asked about future script submissions.\n  - directors: Joanna finished and printed her first full screenplay last Friday, hoping directors and producers will like it enough for it to be produced.\n  - dialogues exploring loss, redemption, and forgiveness: Joanna mentioned a page with dialogues exploring loss, redemption, and forgiveness for her next movie; she finds the story deep and emotional.\n  - a person: Joanna experienced seeing characters and dialogue she wrote acted out, calling it an amazing and rewarding experience that was the third time this has happened.\n  - third: Joanna asked Nate what made him get a 'third' after he mentioned not making it to the finals of a game tournament.\n  - characters: Joanna saw characters she wrote acted out on the big screen for the third time, finding the experience rewarding. Nate inquired about the character on the left in a shared photo.\n  - movie: Joanna is filming her movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and enjoys showing her vision, with Nate asking about the coolest moment.\n  - new opportunities: Joanna expressed hope that finishing her first screenplay would lead to new opportunities and positive feedback.\n  - new things: Joanna submitted a screenplay to a film contest and mentioned that people love it when she makes them new things.\n  - positive feedback: Joanna hopes finishing her first screenplay will lead to positive feedback and new opportunities.\n  - director: Joanna hopes a director falls in love with her screenplay to get it on the big screen.\n  - dialogue: Joanna found it rewarding to see the dialogue she wrote acted out, noting it was the third time this happened. Seeing characters and dialogue from her writing performed was an amazing experience.\n  - Real-life stories: Nate mentioned that real-life stories are the best for inspiration and looks forward to hearing about Joanna's next one.\n  - book: Joanna finished writing and editing her bo