eceiving love and support. Evan feels lucky to have found someone who gets them, strengthening their bond.\n  - someone who gets Evan: Evan's partner is someone who gets Evan, and Evan feels lucky to have found them. Evan and their partner announced their marriage to their extended family.\n  - Evan: Evan married his partner last week. Evan was asked by Sam if his spouse is the woman from Canada. Evan had previously mentioned enjoying books, painting, driving, and hiking.\n  - Evan: Evan's partner understood his accidental damage to rose bushes. He also enjoys yoga for stress/flexibility and rewatching The Godfather; he previously drank too much with friends.\n  - Evan: Evan told his extended family about his marriage and plans to try poutine in Canada next month. He told Sam he had too much to drink last night and did something regrettable involving roses.\n  - Evan: Evan told Sam about an incident from the previous night where he drank too much and something involving someone's roses occurred.\n  - Evan: Evan told Sam he is in love at first sight with a woman from Canada and expressed regret for not marrying her sooner.\n  - Evan's family: Evan told his extended family about his marriage yesterday; the family showed love and support, and is very happy for him and his partner.\n  - Evan: Evan is excited as his partner is pregnant. He looks forward to parenthood, remembering the joy of his first child, and is planning a family reunion next summer.\n  - Evan: Evan told Sam he is in love with a woman from Canada, whom he married, and expressed joy from viewing a painting that helped him recognize his feelings.\n  - Evan: Evan mentioned a minor accident that dampened telling work friends about getting married; they have been very supportive.\n  - Evan: Evan told Sam he is in love with a woman, possibly from Canada, and they did not marry sooner.\n  - Evan: Evan got married last week to the woman from Canada, whom he loved at first sight. He confirmed his love at first sight feeling to Sam.\n  - Evan: Evan informed their extended family about their marriage, receiving a lot of love and support. Evan feels lucky and that their families' happiness is the best part.\n  - Evan: Evan greeted Sam, mentioned taking the Prius for a mountain drive last weekend, and was in a minor accident on the way back. He also shared he got married last week.\n  - Evan: Evan mentioned his son had an accident last Tuesday after falling off his bike and is now doing better. He recently finished a contemporary figurative painting emphasizing emotional state.\n  - woman from Canada: Evan is in love with the woman from Canada, stating he was in love with her at first sight and questioning why they hadn't married sooner.\n  - Evan: Evan encouraged Sam about starting a diet and living healthier, praising Sam's determination and asking about positive changes.\n  - Evan: Evan congratulated Sam on becoming a Weight Watchers coach. Evan shared a picture taken last Friday at a favorite beach spot where he watches waves and sunsets to find peace.\n  - Evan: Evan plans to go on a hike with Sam soon. He recently returned from a morning walk, which he finds helps start the day actively.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2059,"context_chars":8357,"retrieval_duration":0.21886014938354492,"response_duration":2.139374256134033,"total_duration":2.358234405517578,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer mentions the drunken night as the reason for Evan's apology, which aligns with the gold answer.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides all necessary information to answer the question about why Evan apologized to his partner. It explicitly states that Evan apologized for a drunken night, which directly aligns with the golden answer. Additionally, the context includes details about the incident and Evan's feelings of embarrassment, confirming the reason for the apology.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["Evan apologized to their partner","The drunken night caused Evan to apologize","Evan felt embarrassed the morning after going out"]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_3","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_3_qa_99","category":"4","difficulty":"unknown","query":"What are Joanna's plans for her finished screenplay in January 2022?","golden_answer":"submit it to film festivals and get producers and directors to check it out","hypothesis":"In January 2022, Joanna's plans for her finished screenplay included submitting it to film festivals, hoping for positive feedback, and seeking new opportunities stemming from the screenplay. She also intended for producers and directors to check out her screenplay. These plans were articulated on January 23, 2022.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of when the fact was stated.\n# Timestamps in memories represent the actual time the event occurred, not the time the event was mentioned in a message.\n\n<FACTS>\n  - Joanna hopes her screenplay gets noticed and makes it to the screen. (event_time: 2022-02-25T13:07:00Z)\n  - Joanna hopes for positive feedback regarding her completed screenplay. (event_time: 2022-01-23T14:01:00Z)\n  - Joanna hopes for new opportunities stemming from her completed screenplay. (event_time: 2022-01-23T14:01:00Z)\n  - Joanna hopes her screenplay ends up on the big screen. (event_time: 2022-02-07T09:27:00Z)\n  - Joanna plans to submit the screenplay to film festivals (event_time: 2022-01-23T14:01:00Z)\n  - Joanna created a plan for getting the script made into a movie (event_time: 2022-11-09T17:54:00Z)\n  - Nate asked Joanna if she has any new plans for the screenplay. (event_time: 2022-01-23T14:01:0