ong with coconut milk, vanilla extract, and salt.\n  - ice cream: Joanna thanked Nate for offering mouthwatering ice cream.\n  - Nate: Nate congratulated Joanna on filming her movie from the road-trip script and asked about the coolest moment on set. He previously tried making coconut ice cream and had a game tournament pushed back.\n  - something delicious: Nate invited Joanna to try something super yummy that he made yesterday.\n  - dairy-free vanilla with strawberry filling and coconut cream frosting: Joanna likes the item described as dairy-free vanilla with strawberry filling and coconut cream frosting, referencing a past coconut recommendation from Nate.\n  - recipe: Joanna has a tasty recipe she is perfecting; she previously shared a dessert recipe with blueberries, coconut milk, and a gluten-free crust. Nate suggested trying this recipe.\n  - mixed berry flavors: Nate enjoys mixed berry flavors, in addition to coconut milk and chocolate.\n  - dairy-free: Joanna likes dairy-free desserts, especially those made with almond milk. Nate previously taught vegan ice cream recipes on his cooking show.\n  - vegan ice cream recipes: Nate taught people vegan ice cream recipes on his cooking show last Monday, finding it nerve-wracking but fun, and he learned new recipes.\n  - Nate: Nate congratulated Joanna on filming her movie from her road-trip script, asked about the coolest on-set moment, and commented that her food looked yummy with nice colors and kick.\n  - salt: Salt was used as an ingredient, along with coconut milk, vanilla extract, and sugar, to make ice cream.\n  - desserts I bake: Joanna has been making all sorts of desserts (cookies, pies, cakes) that suit everyone's diets and will share more recipes with Nate soon. Nate previously made chocolate and vanilla swirl desserts and values Joanna's enjoyment.\n  - new one: Nate asked Joanna about the topic of the \"new one\" after mentioning he baked desserts and made ice cream for a friend.\n  - dairy-free chocolate mousse: Nate likes dairy-free chocolate mousse because it is super creamy and tastes like the real thing.\n  - desserts: Joanna will bring some of her dessert recipes to share with Nate, building on a prior conversation where they discussed dairy-free dessert recipes.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2018,"context_chars":8179,"retrieval_duration":0.1858682632446289,"response_duration":3.167903423309326,"total_duration":3.353771686553955,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer mentions that Nate described the coconut milk ice cream as rich and creamy, which aligns with the gold answer's description.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides all the necessary information to answer the question about Nate's opinion on the coconut milk ice cream he made. It explicitly states that Nate described the ice cream as 'rich and creamy,' which aligns perfectly with the golden answer. Additionally, it mentions that he felt proud of making it and that it turned out pretty good, further supporting his positive opinion. Therefore, the context is sufficient to fully answer the question.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["Nate felt proud of himself for making coconut milk ice cream","Nate described the coconut milk ice cream as rich and creamy","Nate thought the ice cream turned out pretty good"]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_7","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_7_qa_124","category":"4","difficulty":"unknown","query":"How does Jolene plan to pursue her dream of learning to surf?","golden_answer":"gathering information, watching videos, getting a beginners' guide","hypothesis":"Jolene plans to pursue her dream of learning to surf by gathering information, watching videos, and using a beginners' guide to surfing. She is also focused on finding the right time and place to get a surfing lesson and is determined to make an effort to engage in surfing. Additionally, she is currently concentrating